Phase 4.1 — repository picker (recent repos, clone by URL, per-task base branch)
========================================================================
Phase context: Future-tasks Phase 4 item 1 ("the desktop a user can run")
Revision: the Phase 4.1 commits on main (see the phase table row)
Environment: macOS darwin 25.5.0 arm64, local dev profile, UTC

WHAT CHANGED (audit class before: the daemon could run tasks against
exactly ONE ambient repository — MODBIT_REPO_ROOT — read once from the
environment; no registry, no clone, no per-task repo or branch)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- modbit-git: `clone(url, into)` (real git clone; refuses a non-empty
  target) and `worktree_add_from(path, branch, start_point)` (worktrees
  branch FROM a chosen base instead of HEAD). `default_branch()` reads
  HEAD's symbolic ref.
- event-store: migration v6 adds the `recent_repos` registry table
  (docs/31 § Runtime configuration tables); `repos.rs` register/touch/
  list/get. Runtime configuration state — NOT event history, never a
  durability dependency of runs.
- domain: `CreateTask` + `TaskCreated` carry optional `repo_id` and
  `base_branch` (serde defaults keep pre-Phase-4 events deserializable).
- surface.proto (15 → 17 requests): `RegisterRepoCommand`
  (path XOR clone_url), `ListRecentReposRequest`, `RecentRepoView`,
  `RecentRepoList`; `CreateTaskCommand` gains repo_id/base_branch;
  `SurfaceResponse` gains recent_repos/repo. TS bindings regenerated
  (zero-drift CI check applies).
- surface dispatch: RegisterRepo registers an existing local repo OR
  clones the URL into `<worktree_root>/registered/<name>` (real git
  clone transport), captures the repo's default branch, persists the
  registry row; ListRecentRepos lists MRU-first.
- scheduler: tasks naming a registered repo allocate their worktree
  from THAT repo, branching from the requested base (or the repo
  default) via worktree_add_from — per-task base branch selection.
  Without MODBIT_REPO_ROOT the scheduler still has a worktree ROOT
  (DefaultWorktreeRoot source from MODBIT_WORKTREE_ROOT): tasks WITHOUT
  a registered repo then fail with the typed no-repository message.
- DEFECT FIXED (surfaced by the E2E): a run_task error BEFORE the run
  starts (unknown repo id, no configured source) left the task Running
  forever — the poller now transitions it durably with FailTask
  (failure_code run_allocation_failed), so it can never hang.
- desktop: the composer gains the repository picker — recent repos
  dropdown (ListRecentRepos), register-by-path / clone-by-URL inputs
  (RegisterRepo), and a per-task base-branch field. The bridge
  (preload/main/surface-client/bridge-schema) exposes the typed
  RPCs with the same renderer-message schema guard (unknown fields
  rejected; path traversal rejected; exactly-one-of path/cloneUrl).
  TS types exported from @modbit/surface-protocol.

PROOFS (full workspace suite exit 0, 500+ Rust tests; desktop vitest
36 tests green; tsc clean)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
repo_picker_e2e (REAL daemon, REAL git, scripted model):
  registered_repos_drive_task_worktrees_with_base_branches ... ok
  - register-by-path captures default branch "main"
  - register-by-URL (a local path URL) performs a REAL git clone into
    <worktree_root>/registered/<name>
  - the picker list returns both repos with ids
  - the task pinned to repo A + base branch feature/edge runs in a
    worktree on branch modbit/<task12> whose content is checked out
    FROM feature/edge (the edge file exists ONLY on that branch — main
    never sees it, so a HEAD-based worktree would fail this assertion)
  - the registry is durable across a core restart on the same DB
  - an UNKNOWN repo id: the task FAILS durably (run_allocation_failed)
    instead of hanging or silently running against another repository
  - the daemon booted with NO MODBIT_REPO_ROOT: the picker path does
    not need the ambient env var
  desktop bridge tests: createTask repo fields ride the schema guard
  (optional, length-bounded), repo:register exactly-one-of + traversal
  rejection, repo:list shape.

MUTATION CHECK (docs/55), against the Phase 4.1 commit:
  Mutation: per-task base-branch selection disabled (start_point
  forced None) -> repo_picker_e2e FAILED at "the base branch's file is
  checked out" — a HEAD-based worktree lacks the edge-only file, so the
  selection is load-bearing and observable. REVERTED; post-revert E2E
  green. (The unknown-repo failure transition was itself a defect FIX
  proven by the E2E: the pre-fix behavior hung the task Running
  forever.)

CI: run 34498648352 GREEN on all 3 OS (main @ 67badce). Two CI catches
fixed en route, both recorded deliberately: (a) newer clippy denies
io::Lines::flatten in the E2E stderr drain; (b) windows-latest caught
clone-URL backslash handling — a backslash URL made Path::join resolve
the clone target to the SOURCE path itself; the resolver now normalizes
separators before deriving the clone directory (regression covered by
the same E2E).

REMAINING GAPS (Phase 4)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Items 2-6: settings screen, keychain SecretBroker, packaging/signing,
headless CLI, quick-start docs. Clone-by-URL currently supports the
 transports the system git supports (https/ssh use the user's
credentials setup; no bundled credential prompt yet — settings screen
item 2 owns provider/credential UX).
